---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Pricing"
  description="Planned Kitewell launch pricing: one project with up to 10 workflows free, or up to ten projects of 200 workflows with alerts on Kitewell Pro for $15 per month."
>
  <section class="page wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Planned launch pricing</p>
    <h1>One project, free.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A project keeps its workflows, run history, and secrets separate. Both
      plans include the same workflow tools; Pro adds room for more work and
      alerts when it needs you.
    </p>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Free</h2>
        <div class="price">$0</div>
        <ul>
          <li>One project with up to 10 workflows</li>
          <li>Visual workflows and YAML</li>
          <li>Schedules, run history, and event handlers</li>
          <li>AI tasks, MCP, and API access</li>
          <li>No Kitewell account required</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/getting-started/">
          Read the getting started guide
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="card pro">
        <h2>Pro</h2>
        <div class="price">
          $15 <span>/ month · USD</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Up to ten projects, 200 workflows each</li>
          <li>
            Alerts by desktop notification, email, Slack, Microsoft Teams,
            PagerDuty, or webhook
          </li>
          <li>Every feature in Free</li>
          <li>Dagu Cloud account required for the subscription</li>
          <li>
            Existing projects and workflows keep running if Pro lapses; alerts
            stop
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="fine">Purchase will be available with the public launch.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Costs outside Kitewell</h2>
      <p>
        AI provider usage, third-party subscriptions, and infrastructure costs
        are separate. Kitewell does not include AI credits or a hosted computer
        to run your workflows.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/docs/ai/">Learn how AI tasks connect →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
